{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tt-a1i/archify/pulls/289","id":4435602254,"node_id":"PR_kwDOSDCHbc8AAAABCGHrTg","html_url":"https://github.com/tt-a1i/archify/pull/289","diff_url":"https://github.com/tt-a1i/archify/pull/289.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/tt-a1i/archify/pull/289.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tt-a1i/archify/issues/289","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tt-a1i/archify/pulls/289/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tt-a1i/archify/pulls/289/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tt-a1i/archify/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tt-a1i/archify/issues/289/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tt-a1i/archify/statuses/0e43e9d471ee80b12cf9de835f413b35f90120f4","number":289,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"feat(viewer): make story and journey autoplay dwell authorable","user":{"login":"SomSamantray","id":92726151,"node_id":"U_kgDOBYbjhw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92726151?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SomSamantray","html_url":"https://github.com/SomSamantray","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SomSamantray/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SomSamantray/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SomSamantray/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SomSamantray/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SomSamantray/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SomSamantray/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SomSamantray/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SomSamantray/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SomSamantray/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Problem and value\n\nFixes #57.\n\nBoth autoplay dwell constants in the delivered viewer were hardcoded at `1100`, and neither was authorable. `storyBeatDwell()` takes the max of that floor and `viewInterval / beatCount`, so for a story of three or more beats the floor always won and every beat got exactly 1.1s regardless of how much content it carries. The only workaround was patching the installed `assets/template.html` and re-delivering every diagram, which does not survive a skill upgrade.\n\nDiagrams can now author playback pacing directly. `meta.motion.dwell` carries optional `storyFollowMinMs`, `journeyStepMs`, and `viewIntervalMs` values (integers, 1100-60000ms) that reach the delivered page as a JSON data block and drive the story and journey schedulers. Authoring nothing keeps today's exact 1100/3200 defaults and byte-identical rendering.\n\n## Scope\n\n- What changed:\n  - `meta.motion` added to the shared schema `$defs` and referenced from all five diagram types; standalone validators regenerated.\n  - `writeDiagram`/`applyTemplate` emit an optional `archify-motion-data` JSON block; authored-less renders emit no block.\n  - The viewer resolves the block once at boot into `Archify.motionConfig`; the guided-story and route-journey schedulers read their timing from it, keeping the readability floor as the fallback.\n  - New `autoplay-dwell.test.mjs` regression covering all five renderers (authored, absent, partial, out-of-bounds); three pinned literal assertions rebased onto the authored-default shape.\n- What deliberately did not change: the 1100ms/3200ms defaults, the `max(floor, interval/count)` story-dwell formula, camera-settle design, route animation durations, and the schema-v1 typed JSON contract (the addition is optional and additive).\n- No unrelated changes: confirmed. Every file in the diff serves the dwell contract or is a regenerated artifact of the template change.\n\n## Stability impact\n\n- Compatibility and migration risk: low. Existing schema-v1 documents validate identically (verified against all five checked-in examples with and without `meta.motion`). Artifacts without `meta.motion` render byte-identically modulo the timing-code region of the embedded template.\n- Renderer, validator, package, or generated-artifact risk: standalone validators are regenerated from the schemas (`check:validators` green). A corrupt or hand-edited motion block degrades to the floor defaults instead of killing the viewer boot script (guarded; browser-verified with a literal `null` block).\n- Failure behavior and rollback path: out-of-bounds dwell values fail schema validation with a machine-readable diagnostic before delivery. Rollback is a plain revert; no data or format migration is involved.\n\n## Tests run\n\n```\ncd archify && npm test\n# tests 1030 | pass 1003 | fail 0 | skipped 27 (browser-gated, no ARCHIFY_CHROME in runner)\n\nnode --test test/autoplay-dwell.test.mjs\n# tests 4 | pass 4 | fail 0\n\nnode --test test/story-follow-camera.test.mjs test/route-journey.test.mjs \\\n  test/guided-views.test.mjs test/story-trail.test.mjs test/story-beat-navigator.test.mjs\n# tests 30 | pass 30 | fail 0\n\nnode bin/archify.mjs validate architecture <motion-fixture>.json --json   # exit 0\nnode bin/archify.mjs validate architecture <storyFollowMinMs:10>.json --json\n# exit 1 — schema/minimum: /meta/motion/dwell/storyFollowMinMs must be >= 1100\n```\n\n`npm test` includes `check:validators`, `test/golden.mjs`, gallery freshness, and the version-sync gates. Browser verification (Chrome, real playback): authored dwell held beat 1/5 past the 1.2s mark and advanced to 2/5 at ~2.2s, matching the authored 2000ms floor; a hand-tampered `null` motion block degraded to the 1100/3200 defaults with the viewer fully alive.\n\n## Visual evidence\n\nStatic rendering is unchanged by design (geometry/layout verified byte-identical in the regenerated goldens; zero geometry-touching diff lines). Visual review of the delivered page: passed — diagram, guided-views panel, and playback all render and animate correctly in Chrome with authored, corrupt, and absent motion blocks. No layout or visual regression observed.\n\n## Generated artifacts\n\nRegenerated because the viewer template changed (authoritative inputs listed per `CONTRIBUTING.md`):\n\n- `archify/examples/*.html` (5) and `examples/*.html` mirrors (5) + `examples/web-app.html`\n- `examples/checkout-platform-delta.html` + `.receipt.json`\n- `docs/gallery/*` (11 artifacts) + `docs/gallery/manifest.json` + `docs/gallery.html`\n- `docs/assets/archify-live-proof.gif` + `.json` (54 frames / 5.4s — visual proof content unchanged, only embedded template bytes)\n- `archify.zip` (rebuilt with Node 22, byte-reproducibility gate green)\n\n## Unapplied review findings\n\nResiduals from the pre-ship review (run 20260903-214252-3c7dcf46) that need a maintainer decision; finding #1 (corrupt-block guard) was applied in this PR.\n\n- [ ] P3 — `archify/SKILL.md` — `meta.motion` has no author-facing documentation or changelog entry; add a SKILL.md bullet, schemas/README paragraph, authoring-contract section, and CHANGELOG entry (suggested fix in review).\n- [ ] P3 — `archify/test/autoplay-dwell.test.mjs` — runtime wiring is proven only by source-shape regexes; a DOM-shimmed execution probe of the resolver would close the gap a DEFAULTS-mapping typo could slip through.\n- Residual (informational): authored `storyFollowMinMs` above the default `viewIntervalMs` lets the floor dominate short chapters — the documented `max()` semantics; a cross-field validation rule is the alternative if that surprise is unwanted.\n- Residual (informational): authoring any `meta.motion` lowers the attainable `viewIntervalMs` minimum from 3200 to the shared 1100 floor; worth a line in the contract docs either way.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] I used a minimal focused change and preserved existing typed JSON behavior unless the issue requires a contract change.\n- [x] I ran the relevant targeted tests and `npm test` in `archify/`.\n- [x] I added or updated a regression test for behavioral changes.\n- [x] I checked generated artifacts and package freshness when their sources changed.\n- [x] I removed secrets, private repository content, and customer data from fixtures and screenshots.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-09-03T18:03:31Z","updated_at":"2026-09-16T19:00:01Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":null,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"SomSamantray:fix/issue-57-autoplay-dwell","ref":"fix/issue-57-autoplay-dwell","repo":{"id":1356061593,"node_id":"R_kgDOUNPbmQ","name":"archify","full_name":"SomSamantray/archify","owner":{"login":"SomSamantray","id":92726151,"node_id":"U_kgDOBYbjhw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92726151?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SomSamantray","html_url":"https://github.com/SomSamantray","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SomSamantray/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SomSamantray/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SomSamantray/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SomSamantray/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SomSamantray/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SomSamantray/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SomSamantray/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SomSamantray/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SomSamantray/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"private":false,"fork":true,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"description":"Agent skill for beautiful, verifiable architecture, workflow, sequence, data-flow, and lifecycle diagrams—self-contained HTML with motion and crisp export.","homepage":"https://tt-a1i.github.io/archify/","language":null,"visibility":"public","is_template":fa